      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly support the general characterization that a confounding variable is any factor “making it hard to tell which one is actually causing the observed effect.”",
        "While the packet states that prior studies “confound word order with frequency” (because patient-first structures tend to be infrequent), it does not support the definition’s additional phrasing that “frequency can act as a confounding variable if differences attributed to word order might instead be due to how common the sentence structure is.”"
